   $q$Two fractions both have a denominator of $12$. Their sum is $1\frac{1}{12}$ and their difference is $\frac{5}{12}$. What are the two fractions?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{8}{12}$ and $\\frac{5}{12}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"checked-sum-only"},{"text":"$\\frac{13}{12}$ and $\\frac{5}{12}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-the-given-sum-and-difference"},{"text":"$\\frac{10}{12}$ and $\\frac{5}{12}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"checked-difference-only"},{"text":"$\\frac{9}{12}$ and $\\frac{4}{12}$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{9}{12}$ and $\frac{4}{12}$$q$, $q$The sum $1\frac{1}{12}$ is $\frac{13}{12}$, so the numerators add to $13$ and differ by $5$. Trying pairs that add to $13$: $9 + 4 = 13$ and $9 - 4 = 5$. So the fractions are $\frac{9}{12}$ and $\frac{4}{12}$. The pair $\frac{8}{12}$ and $\frac{5}{12}$ has the right sum, but its difference is only $\frac{3}{12}$.$q$, 'draft', null)
